==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} ''[[#Old Norse|fjórir]]'', from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|fedwōr|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{termx||kʷetwṓr|lang=ine-pro}}, the neuter form of {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{recons|kʷetwóres|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Number===
'''fjórir''' {{m|p}}, '''[[fjórar]]''' {{f|p}}, '''[[fjögur]]''' {{n|p}}

# '''[[four]]'''; the cardinal number after [[þrír#Icelandic|þrír]] and before [[fimm#Icelandic|fimm]].
#: ''[[sjá|Sjáðu]]! '''Fjórir''' [[maður#Icelandic|menn]].''
#:: [[look|Look]]! '''Four''' [[man|men]].

====Declension====
{{is-numeral (fjórir)|}}

====Related terms====
* {{qualifier|ordinal form}} [[fjórði]] {{m}}, [[fjórða]] {{f|n}}

====Derived terms====
* [[klukkan fjögur]]
* [[undir fjögur augu]]
* [[á fjórum fótum]]

